Gnumeric @VERSION@ - the spreadsheet (GTK 3) for RISC OS

Gnumeric 1.12.57 by the Gnumeric developers (GPL version 2 or 3), on GTK
3 through riscos-gtk's RISC OS backend: hundreds of functions, charts,
and Excel, OpenDocument, Lotus 1-2-3, Quattro Pro, HTML, CSV and text
files.

New in riscos-gtk's public beta: not everything has been tried on RISC OS
yet, so please report what goes wrong (see riscos-gtk's release notes).

Using it
- Run it: Gnumeric opens a new workbook and puts its icon on the icon
  bar. Or drop a spreadsheet on !Gnumeric in a Filer window.
- The icon bar icon: Select brings Gnumeric's window to the front; Menu
  gives Info, Choices... (Gnumeric's Preferences) and Quit.
- Files dropped on the icon bar icon, or CSV files double-clicked in the
  Filer while Gnumeric is loaded, open in a window of their own.
- Click Menu over a window for Gnumeric's menus.
- File > Save As: a RISC OS Save box (the format is chosen from the name,
  e.g. .xlsx, .ods, .csv, .gnumeric); File > Open: an Open box.
- Gnumeric's settings are kept in <Choices$Write>.Gnumeric.
- Help > Contents, and the Help button in Gnumeric's dialogue boxes,
  open its manual (in the application) in your browser.
- SVG pictures can be inserted (Insert > Image) and are shown.

Not in this build: Python and Perl functions and plugins, databases
(GDA), the external linear solvers (glpk, lp_solve).

Messages
Gnumeric's messages go to <Wimp$ScrapDir>.Gnumeric.Log.

Needs
RISC OS 5 on an ARMv7 or later machine (Raspberry Pi 2 or later, ARMX6,
Titanium...), SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later, ARMEABISupport and Iconv
(PackMan). PThreadTicker is included.
Fonts: Gnumeric uses the desktop's own fonts (Homerton, Trinity, Corpus,
and every font on Font$Path: those in !Fonts, and those a font manager
such as Fontastic adds), as the desktop draws them. The first time it
starts it makes copies they can be used from, in
<Choices$Write>.GTK.FontCache (about a second; again only when a font
changes). It also carries DejaVu Sans, and with FontConfig and fonts
from PackMan installed it uses those too, as other FontConfig programs
do. The Log's "fonts:" lines say which fonts it found.

